From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:25:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: put a data-aligned image's x18 trampolines on their
 own page

An image whose .data [data-align] shifted by less than a page has its
x18 trampoline region at offset + image_alloc, which then starts inside
the image's last page. The .data and .tls protections make that page RW,
so the first trampoline call took an EXECUTE fault: vkd3d-proton's
d3d12.dll (arm64ec, shifted +0x2000) crashed Hollow Knight at its first
D3D12 call. Start the region on the page after the image's end; the
allocation already has the extra page for the shift.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-vulkan-d3d11-d3d12.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index fb08d2e..9d134b6 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -10566,7 +10566,14 @@ static inline int mprotect_exec( void *base, size_t size, int unix_prot )
                          * copy diverged from the source and patching it
                          * would emit copy-specific branches — refuse (x18
                          * insns degrade to recoverable runtime faults). */
-                        size_t tramp_pool_off = offset + image_alloc;
+                        /* The page after the image's last one. offset + image_alloc
+                         * is that only when the image starts on a page: [data-align]
+                         * shifts it by less than a page, and the region then began
+                         * inside the image's last page, which the .data/.tls
+                         * protections below make RW, so the first x18 trampoline
+                         * took an EXECUTE fault (vkd3d-proton's d3d12.dll). The
+                         * allocation has the extra page for the shift. */
+                        size_t tramp_pool_off = (offset + image_size + page_size - 1) & ~(page_size - 1);
                         if (tramp_alloc > tramp_prealloc)
                         {
                             dprintf(2, "[x18-tramp] REFUSED: budget 0x%lx > prealloc 0x%lx (source/copy divergence?)\n",
